---
description: Zen of Reticulum gates for mesh-facing design and code. Always on.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `.agents/conventions/reticulum-zen.md` before any mesh-facing design or
code. Naming is where IP-era assumptions sneak into a mesh, because everyone
reaches for DNS as the model.

No root zone, no registrar, no single naming authority. Destination hashes are
identity; names are local labels the user owns. Assume every resolver is
hostile: a record must be verifiable without trusting whoever served it.
Announce candidates carry evidence and are never auto-selected for a client.
Multiple resolvers disagreeing is the design, not a defect.

Before adding a feature, answer: does it work partitioned, can a hostile
resolver use it to make a client accept an address the user did not choose,
does it introduce a party everyone must trust, and is it still honest when two
resolvers disagree?
